<title>USA: Augusta, Ga., visitor bureau criticizes tax hike.</title>
<headline>Augusta, Ga., visitor bureau criticizes tax hike.</headline>
<dateline>AUGUSTA, Ga. 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The board of Georgia's Augusta Metropolitan Convention and Visitors Bureau passed a resolution opposing the city's proposed increase in its hotel bed tax, the Augusta Chronicle said Friday.</p>
<p>Hotel guests currently pay a 5 percent bed tax in addition to the 7 percent sales tax.</p>
<p>The Georgia Golf Hall of Fame and the National Science Center's Fort Discovery have asked the city to raise the bed tax to 6 percent to run their facilities. The move would generate $200,000 a year.</p>
<p>The Augusta City Commission was scheduled to vote on the request earlier this week but delayed the vote for lack of a quorum.</p>
<p>((--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013))</p>
